    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature \u2014 `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given \u2014 with minimal structural impact.\n\n**Changes (5 files, all small/cohesive additions):**\n\n1. **`Salutation.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny cohesive helper (`WMC_other` = 0) mirroring the existing `ContactPreference`/`Locality` derivation classes: `of(owner)` returns `title + \" \" + lastName` or just `lastName`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` annotation delegating the `salutation` field to `Salutation.of(owner)`, following the existing expression-mapping pattern. No method body touched, so `RespondWithOwner`/`ListOwners` (the larger classes) are untouched.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `title` column field plus its getter/setter (new small methods; existing methods unchanged), so the title persists across the separate POST-create and GET requests.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added optional `title` to `OwnerFields` (request input, auto-mapped to the entity by name) and a read-only `salutation` to `Owner` (response).\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql` + `data.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column to the live test schema and one trailing `NULL` per positional seed insert to keep the row counts valid.\n\nI deliberately left the stale `h2`/`mysql`/`postgres` schemas alone \u2014 they already lack `email`, `postcode`, etc. that hsqldb has, so they aren't the live schema and editing them would add file churn for no benefit.\n\nThe behavior is derived at response time by the mapper, so no request-handling pipeline function needed changing.",
